  imagePosition="42% 28%"
>
  <p>
    Fridge capacity is measured in litres, but litres do not tell you whether the appliance will
    fit the kitchen. Width, total depth, door swing, ventilation and the delivery route can rule
    out a model before its internal layout matters.
  </p>
  <p>
    Start with the finished opening and the path into the house. Then compare it with the exact
    manufacturer's planning and installation documents. Fridges with similar capacities can have
    noticeably different external dimensions.
  </p>

  <nav aria-label="Start your fridge comparison">
    <p><strong>What do you need next?</strong> <a href="#fridge-size-chart-heading">Check the size chart</a>, <a href="#fridge-shortlist-route-heading">choose a layout to compare</a> or <a href="#fridge-measurements-heading">measure your opening first</a>.</p>
  </nav>

  <section aria-labelledby="fridge-size-chart-heading">
    <h2 id="fridge-size-chart-heading">Fridge size chart: body dimensions are not cavity sizes</h2>
    <p>There is no single standard fridge size in Australia. These three researched options show why body width alone cannot confirm fit. Measurements below are <strong>width × height × depth</strong>.</p>
    <p class="table-hint">Swipe sideways to compare the full table.</p>
    <div class="comparison-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Fridge sizes in millimetres and centimetres">
      <table class="comparison-table">
        <caption>Three fridge sizes and their model-specific width checks</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model and layout</th><th scope="col">Body dimensions in mm</th><th scope="col">The same size in cm</th><th scope="col">Width including stated side gaps</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#product-lg-gb-b400ps-fridge-fit-good-guys">LG GB-B400PS</a><br />436L bottom freezer</th><td>697 × 1,740 × 696</td><td>69.7 × 174 × 69.6</td><td>705mm (70.5cm), using 4mm each side. A 700mm opening is too narrow.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#product-westinghouse-wtm4302wd-r-good-guys">Westinghouse WTM4302WD-R</a><br />431L top freezer</th><td>699 × 1,725 × 723</td><td>69.9 × 172.5 × 72.3</td><td>759mm (75.9cm), using 30mm each side in the documented arrangement.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#product-tgg-gap-haier-hrf510fhs">Haier HRF510FHS</a><br />509L French door</th><td>790 × 1,725 × 707</td><td>79 × 172.5 × 70.7</td><td>850mm (85cm) in Haier's planning sheet, including 30mm each side.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Those final figures check width only. All three still need rear and overhead ventilation, levelling and door access; a nearby wall may need much more room. Read the <a href="#fridge-shortlist-heading">LG fit notes</a>, <a href="#top-mount-choice-heading">Westinghouse installation notes</a> or <a href="#french-door-choice-heading">Haier planning notes</a> before ordering.</p>
    <p><strong>Working in centimetres?</strong> Multiply by 10 to get millimetres: a 70cm opening is 700mm. A “60cm fridge” or “900mm opening” is only a starting description, not confirmation that an exact model fits.</p>
  </section>

  <MeasurementWorksheetLink appliance="fridge" />

  <section aria-labelledby="fridge-shortlist-route-heading">
    <h2 id="fridge-shortlist-route-heading">Which fridge is worth checking for your kitchen?</h2>
    <p>First rule out models that cannot meet the installation requirements. Then compare where you want the freezer, how much fresh and frozen food you store, and whether a water dispenser is useful.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>Small side gaps and a bottom freezer:</strong> consider the <a href="#product-lg-gb-b400ps-fridge-fit-good-guys">LG GB-B400PS</a>. It has 308L of fridge space and a 128L freezer. Its 705mm width check does not solve a shallow cavity: it still needs more than 50mm behind, overhead space and room to use the doors.</li>
      <li><strong>A top freezer and more fresh-food space than the LG:</strong> compare the <a href="#product-westinghouse-wtm4302wd-r-good-guys">Westinghouse WTM4302WD-R</a>, with a 329L fridge and 102L freezer. Allow for its wider ventilation gaps and right-hinge door; it is not an alternative for the same narrow opening.</li>
      <li><strong>French doors and water without a plumbed connection:</strong> compare the <a href="#product-tgg-gap-haier-hrf510fhs">Haier HRF510FHS</a>, with a 372L fridge and 137L freezer. Start with its 850mm-wide planning cavity, then check both door arcs and drawer access. The water tank needs refilling and cleaning; it does not provide automatic ice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>If none fits, keep looking.</strong> A 700mm opening is too narrow for all three under these width checks. A wider opening alone does not guarantee fit either. Use the <a href="#fridge-measurements-heading">measurement checks below</a> to identify the limiting dimension before choosing another model.</p>
  </section>

  <CommercialProductBlock guidePath="/guides/fridge-dimensions-australia/" title="Compare the three models and check current prices" intro="First compare the fit checks and trade-offs below to narrow your shortlist, then check the exact model's current price and postcode delivery options at the retailer. These are research-based options, not firsthand AHC tests or a promise that a model fits your kitchen." variant="comparison" comparisonDetails={applianceComparisons} />

  <p><strong>Before placing an order:</strong> match the full model code and finish, confirm the installation drawing and delivery route, and compare <a href="#fridge-order-heading">delivery, removal and setup costs</a>. Do not reduce the specified ventilation gaps to make a model fit.</p>

